AlphaFold3 on TPU (Stanford class-tpu-cluster-west4, v5e-8) -- attempt log
============================================================================

Everything up through building the input and installing dependencies
succeeded on the first real attempt:

  + apt-get install (build-essential, cmake, ninja-build, libcifpp deps) -- OK
  + uv sync (AlphaFold3 + CPU/GPU-flavored jaxlib)                        -- OK
  + uv pip install "jax[tpu]==0.10.2" -f libtpu_releases.html             -- OK
  + uv run build_data
      Parsing /alphafold3/.venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/share/libcifpp/components.cif
      Writing /alphafold3/src/alphafold3/constants/converters/ccd.pickle
      Done
      Loading /alphafold3/src/alphafold3/constants/converters/ccd.pickle
      Finding ions and glycans
      writing to /alphafold3/src/alphafold3/constants/converters/chemical_component_sets.pickle
      Done                                                                -- OK
  + weights download + zstd decompress (1146811260 bytes)                 -- OK
  + uv run python3 make_af3_input.py --seed=1
      Wrote /alphafold3/af3_toy_input.json (seed=1, 118 residues)         -- OK

Then the actual inference call:

  $ uv run python3 run_alphafold.py \
      --json_path=/alphafold3/af3_toy_input.json \
      --model_dir=/af3_weights \
      --output_dir=/alphafold3/results/af3_tpu_output \
      --norun_data_pipeline \
      --flash_attention_implementation=xla \
      --jax_backend=tpu

  FATAL Flags parsing error: flag --jax_backend=tpu: value should be one of <cpu|gpu|mps>
  Pass --helpshort or --helpfull to see help on flags.

  real    0m5.588s
  user    0m18.874s
  sys     0m0.447s

Conclusion: every infrastructure step this project's TPU workflow depends
on (native C++ build, Chemical Component Dictionary, weights, input JSON,
even the jax[tpu]/libtpu install) works correctly on this cluster. The
wall this project hit is AlphaFold3's own public CLI: --jax_backend's
enum is <cpu|gpu|mps> -- no 'tpu' value exists to select. This matches
AlphaFold3's official installation docs (An NVIDIA GPU with compute
capability 7.0 or higher is required) and every third-party HPC-center
guide checked for this project, none of which list TPU as a supported
target for the public AlphaFold3 release. See results/sweep/af3_comparison.md
Section 3 for the full writeup.
